22:T11d2,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What credentials does TryTokka store?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"One read-only billing or usage credential per connected provider, and nothing else. TryTokka never receives your prompts, completions, or model traffic â€” it reads spend totals from provider billing endpoints."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are they encrypted at rest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. AES-256-GCM with a random 16-byte IV per row and a stored authentication tag, written as iv:authTag:ciphertext. Tampered ciphertext fails authentication and throws rather than decrypting."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the application recover the plaintext, and when?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and it has to â€” reading your spend means calling the provider with your credential. It is decrypted in server memory during a verification or sync, used for that request, and never written back in plaintext."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the operator read your keys?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No admin or operator screen in the application can display one. But whoever holds the deployment ENCRYPTION_KEY together with database access could decrypt outside the app, so the honest answer is that the capability exists. Every in-app decryption is audited and you can read that log yourself. We keep 90 days of it; download the CSV if you want a longer record, because that copy is yours and does not depend on us."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is provider OAuth used where it exists?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Where a provider offers a scoped cloud identity, yes â€” Google Cloud and Azure connect through service principals that mint short-lived OAuth 2.0 tokens, and AWS uses a scoped IAM user. The other providers publish no OAuth path for billing reads, so TryTokka asks for the narrowest read-only key each one offers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What permissions are requested?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Read-only billing or usage scope, never completion access. TryTokka rejects chat/completion keys by shape where it can detect them, because a key that can read spend should not also be able to spend."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where are the credentials hosted?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Encrypted rows live in Supabase Postgres behind Row-Level Security. Current production compute runs on Vercel in iad1 (Washington, D.C. area, United States). The ENCRYPTION_KEY is supplied through the Vercel environment and is never stored in the database. Region is not customer-selectable; there is no EU-only option today."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is the encryption key rotated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At least every 90 days, and sooner after any suspected environment exposure, using a dual-key window (ENCRYPTION_KEY plus ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS) so existing rows still decrypt. That rotation does not rotate your provider keys â€” you revoke the dedicated TryTokka key in each provider console yourself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do keys survive account deletion?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They go with the account. Connection rows are foreign-keyed to the auth user with ON DELETE CASCADE, so deleting your account removes the encrypted credential in the same transaction. You can also delete a single connection at any time without closing the account. A hash of your email is kept only to block repeating the free trial. Disaster-recovery snapshots can retain encrypted blobs for up to 90 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Has there been an external security audit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No third-party penetration test or external audit has been commissioned. TryTokka is a solo-operated product and does not claim otherwise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there SOC 2 or ISO 27001 certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Neither certification has been obtained. If your procurement process requires one, TryTokka does not currently meet it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if there is an incident?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Suspected incidents are investigated and affected systems contained, with regulator or user notification where applicable law requires it. A user notice would state known impact and recommend revoking affected provider credentials. The procedure is published at /incident-response."}}]}14:["$","$1","c",{"children":[[[["$","script","jsonld-0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"TryTokka Security\",\"description\":\"How TryTokka encrypts and protects AI provider API keys.\",\"url\":\"https://trytokka.com/security\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"TryTokka\",\"url\":\"https://trytokka.com\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"}"}}],["$","script","jsonld-1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://trytokka.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Security\",\"item\":\"https://trytokka.com/security\"}]}"}}],["$","script","jsonld-2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$22"}}]],"$L23"],null,"$L24"]}]
